! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.7, "CUBE ROOT", printed p.31 (PDF 32), read in the
! ink.
!
!   "Program to compute the cube root of a normalized floating-point
!   number N by the following iteration formula:
!     x(k+1) = x(k) (x(k)**3 + 2N) / (2 x(k)**3 + N)
!            = x(k) [ 1/2 + (3N/2) / (2 x(k)**3 + N) ]
!   Use it to compute the cube root of 8, with x(0) = 2.5.  Ten
!   iterations will give full-length accuracy except for the round-off
!   error in the last iteration."
!
!   Method 1
!       CBRT    L(U), EN
!               E -I, 1
!               +(N), EN
!               ST(U), TEMP             '3N/2 stored in TEMP
!               LX, $2, XW2
!               L, GUESS
!       LOOP    ST, XK
!               *, XK
!               *, XK
!               E + I, 1
!               +, EN                   '2X ** 3 + N
!               R/, TEMP
!               +, HALF
!               *, XK                   'new XK created
!               CB, $2, LOOP
!               ST, ANS
!               BEW, $
!       XW2     XW, 0.0, 10, XW2
!       HALF    DD(N), 0.5
!       ANS     DR(N), (1)
!       TEMP    DR(N), (2)
!       XK      SYN (N), TEMP + 1.0
!       EN      DD(N), 8.0
!       GUESS   DD(N), 2.5
!
! The twenty-four printed statements are the deck's last twenty-four, as
! printed, data and all, with the page's own spacing ("E -I, 1",
! "E + I, 1", "SYN (N), TEMP + 1.0").  BLOCK A before them is the deck's
! copy of the seventeen instructions, the BEW left off, every symbol
! with an A appended, and its own constants written 8, 5/2 and 1/2,
! which the assembler makes exact.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2: strap_asm.py refuses "L, GUESS" and the
! eight others like it (decks/problem_3_bare_op_symbol_dds.strap).  By
! C22-6578 printed p.30 comment (c) every bare operation here takes (N)
! from its symbol, and "E -I" and "E + I", which name no symbol, take
! (U).
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE DERIVED FROM THE MANUAL'S RULES, NOT FROM THE
! MODEL, by tests/problem_3_expected.py (p37), rules and pages in its
! header; eighty truncating steps.  What is checkable by hand is:
!
!   BLOCK A, exact 8, 2.5 and .5:
!     2 is a fixed point of the printed sequence with nothing to
!     truncate: 2 x 2 x 2 = 8; E+I, 1 doubles it, 16; + 8 = 24;
!     12 / 24 = .5; + .5 = 1; x 2 = 2.  The iteration converges
!     cubically from 2.5 (comment (a)), so ten steps arrive:
!       ANSA  = 2    0048000000000000
!       XKA   = 2    0048000000000000   (the tenth iteration's input:
!                                       it was already there)
!       TEMPA = 12   008C000000000000   3N/2 = 4 + 8
!
!   THE PAGE, with 8.0, 2.5 and 0.5 as the host STRAP II makes them,
!   each one unit of its 48th place short (8 - 2**-45, 2.5 - 2**-46,
!   .5 - 2**-49; see problem_3_4_method1.strap):
!     TEMP by hand: L(U), EN is 8 - 2**-45; E-I, 1 halves it, 4 -
!     2**-46; + EN is 12 - 3 x 2**-46.  A number with exponent 4 has
!     2**-44 for its 48th place, so that is 12 less three quarters of
!     a unit, truncated to 12 less one unit:
!       TEMP  = 008BFFFFFFFFFFF0
!     The cube root of 8 - 2**-45 is 2 - 2**-45/12, a third of a unit
!     below 2, which truncates to 2 less one unit.  The program gets
!       ANS   = 002FFFFFFFFFFFE0        2 less two units
!       XK    = 002FFFFFFFFFFFE0
!     -- one unit further off, which is the page's own "except for the
!     round-off error in the last iteration".  The exact words are the
!     calculator's.
!     EN_as_assembled 006FFFFFFFFFFFF0, GUESS_as_assembled
!     0049FFFFFFFFFFF0, HALF_as_assembled 003FFFFFFFFFFFF0.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): "ENA DD(N), 8" changed to "ENA DD(N), 27".
! FAIL A_ANS, A_XK and A_TEMP; the six checks of the page's own block
! and the PC passed.  (A_ANS came back 004C000000000000: 3, the cube
! root of 27.)

! --- block A: the deck's copy, exact constants ------------------------
CBRTA   L(U), ENA
        E -I, 1
        +(N), ENA
        ST(U), TEMPA
        LX, $2, XW2A
        L, GUESSA
LOOPA   ST, XKA
        *, XKA
        *, XKA
        E + I, 1
        +, ENA
        R/, TEMPA
        +, HALFA
        *, XKA
        CB, $2, LOOPA
        ST, ANSA
! --- the page, as printed -------------------------------------------
CBRT    L(U), EN
        E -I, 1
        +(N), EN
        ST(U), TEMP
        LX, $2, XW2
        L, GUESS
LOOP    ST, XK
        *, XK
        *, XK
        E + I, 1
        +, EN
        R/, TEMP
        +, HALF
        *, XK
        CB, $2, LOOP
        ST, ANS
        BEW, $
XW2     XW, 0.0, 10, XW2
HALF    DD(N), 0.5
ANS     DR(N), (1)
TEMP    DR(N), (2)
XK      SYN (N), TEMP + 1.0
EN      DD(N), 8.0
GUESS   DD(N), 2.5
! --- block A's data -------------------------------------------------
XW2A    XW, 0.0, 10, XW2A
HALFA   DD(N), 1/2
ANSA    DR(N), (1)
TEMPA   DR(N), (2)
XKA     SYN (N), TEMPA + 1.0
ENA     DD(N), 8
GUESSA  DD(N), 5/2
        END, CBRTA
